Modifications in this repository integrate native ModelOpt/Marlin checkpoint
layouts, model-bound configuration and fingerprint isolation, bounded
stream/graph-owned workspaces, complete-tie sampling eligibility, and
QWEN-EXO PLE/observer boundaries rather than workstation-specific extensions
or process-global monkeypatch registries.

Upstream notice retained for attribution:

Qwen3.8-Flash-Next RTX PRO 6000 runtime configuration and measurements
Copyright 2026 SSHdotCodes contributors

serve/overlays/sglang contains modified SGLang 0.5.20 source, distributed
under Apache-2.0. Upstream: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
Modifications: SM120 QSA/FP8 handling, pending-ring storage and indexing,
draft vocabulary selection, proposal-probability lifetime, and startup loading.
See the upstream serve/runtime.json for the immutable base and installed hashes.

The upstream numeric draft token map derives from the public hot_tokens_64k.pt
artifact in https://github.com/gabrielolympie/sglang-flashnext-sm120 with all
Qwen special IDs included. Provenance and source checksum: upstream docs/runtime.md.
That map is not incorporated by this adaptation; target and proposal tensors
retain the full native vocabulary. No model weights are redistributed here.
